  "body": "Slice A of the three in `docs/adr/0004-host-control-sliced-delivery.md`. No dependencies; slices B (#110) and C (#111) follow in parallel. **Size: M.** Tier: `fast`. The choices below are decisions you can overturn.

## Wire contract

- JSON over HTTP with `Content-Type: application/json`. Bodies are at most 64 KiB and connections use `Connection: close`.
- Every request carries an integer `protocolVersion`, which only a breaking change bumps. A mismatch fails with `unsupported_protocol_version`. Paths are unversioned.
- Results use the Runtime Upload POST shape.
- Command names are flat camelCase (`capabilities`, `echo`, later `mediaPlayPause`), so `host.<name>()` is a single mapped type.

```jsonc
// Command: Vita → companion, POST {url}command
{ "protocolVersion": 1, "command": "echo", "payload": { "text": "hi" } }
// 200 { "ok": true, "text": "hi" }
// 422 { "ok": false, "code": "invalid_payload", "message": "echo needs a string text." }

// Link: companion → Vita, POST http://<vita>:<port>/link
{ "protocolVersion": 1, "name": "Studio Mac", "url": "http://192.168.1.20:8797/" }
// 200 { "ok": true }
```

`HostControlErrorCode` has two groups:

- **Wire:** `malformed_request`, `unsupported_protocol_version`, `unknown_command`, `invalid_payload`, `forbidden`, `unsupported_platform`, `command_failed`, `payload_too_large`.
- **Client-only:** `not_linked`, `unreachable`, `timeout`, `bad_response`.

If the client receives a code it doesn't know, it reports `command_failed` and keeps the companion's message.

## SDK

A new subpath export, `@vitadeck/sdk/host-control` (`js/packages/sdk/src/host-control/`). One registry serves both sides:

```ts
export const hostCommands = defineHostCommands({
  capabilities: command<undefined, HostCapabilities>(isAbsent),
  echo: command<{ text: string }, { text: string }>(isEchoPayload),
});

export type HostResult<R> =
  | ({ ok: true } & R)
  | { ok: false; code: HostControlErrorCode; message: string };

// In a Deck App
import { host } from "@vitadeck/sdk/host-control";
const reply = await host.echo({ text: "hi" });
if (reply.ok) console.log(reply.text);
else if (reply.code === "not_linked") setHint("Link a computer in the Shell");
```

- **Validation.** Entries are phantom-typed. The companion validates each payload with that entry's guard. There is no schema library, since one would ship inside every Deck App bundle.
- **Defining commands.** `defineHostCommands` stays internal. Authors call commands but don't define them, because the companion is VitaDeck-owned in v1.
- **Capabilities.** `HostCapabilities.commands` is a `string[]`, since a newer companion may list commands this SDK doesn't know.
- **Errors.** Methods resolve to a `HostResult` and never reject for a Host Control failure, so TypeScript forces the `ok` check.
- **Offline.** The default `host` reads `nativeGetHostControlUrl()` (slice C) on every call. If the function is missing or returns `""`, the call fails with `not_linked` without using the network. A refused connection gives `unreachable`. There are no retries, because a retried launch would launch twice. `createHostClient({ url, transport, timeoutMs })` builds a client for tests.
- **Timeout.** It defaults to 5 s as a `setTimeout` race, since the Vita `fetch` has no `AbortSignal`. libcurl runs on until its 30 s cap, so a `timeout` means the command may still have run.
- **Bundling.** The CLI's rolldown `external` lists only the bare `@vitadeck/sdk`, so this subpath is bundled into each Deck App. The VitaDeck Runtime Bundle stays untouched, and each app keeps the protocol version it was built with.

## Tests

- `src/host-control/*.test.ts` run against a fake transport: the envelope, every error mapping, timeout, and not linked. A new `test:sdk` script runs them, and it joins the `fast` tier.
- A CLI test builds a Deck App that imports the subpath.
- Contract fixtures in `tests/fixtures/host-control/*.json`, each a `{ request, status, response }` triple: link ok, link version mismatch, capabilities, echo, unknown command, invalid payload. The SDK tests, slice B, and slice C's C harness all replay the same bytes.

**Files:** `js/packages/sdk/src/host-control/{index,commands,client}.ts` and their tests, `js/packages/sdk/package.json`, `js/packages/sdk/README.md`, `tests/fixtures/host-control/`, `scripts/agent-check.sh`.

Posted by Claude Code [claude-opus-5-5]
",

